#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm"
msgstr "Ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm outperforms all classical algorithms for a query problem, but the advantage is quite modest: one query versus two.\n"
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm extends this advantage — and, in fact, it can be used to solve a couple of different query problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang algorithm ni Deutsch ay mas mahusay kaysa sa lahat ng classical algorithm para sa isang query problem, ngunit maliit lamang ang kalamangan: isa kumpara sa dalawang query.\n"
"Pinapalawig ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm ang kalamantang ito — at, sa katunayan, maaari itong gamitin para malutas ang ilang iba't ibang query problem.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a quantum circuit description of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"An additional classical post-processing step, not shown in the figure, may also be required depending on the specific problem being solved.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang quantum circuit na paglalarawan ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"Maaaring kailanganin din ang karagdagang classical post-processing na hakbang, na hindi ipinapakita sa figure, depende sa partikular na problemang nilulutas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, we haven't actually discussed what problems this algorithm solves; this is done in the two sections that follow.\n"
msgstr "Siyempre, hindi pa natin tinalakay kung anong mga problema ang nilulutas ng algorithm na ito; gagawin ito sa dalawang seksyong susunod.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa problem {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"
msgstr "Ang Deutsch-Jozsa problem {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll begin with the query problem the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm was originally intended to solve, which is known as the *Deutsch-Jozsa problem*.\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo sa query problem na orihinal na layunin ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm na malutas, na kilala bilang ang *Deutsch-Jozsa problem*.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The input function for this problem takes the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ for an arbitrary positive integer $n$.\n"
"Like Deutsch's problem, the task is to output $0$ if $f$ is constant and $1$ if $f$ is balanced, which again means that the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $0$ is equal to the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang input function para sa problemang ito ay may anyo na $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ para sa isang arbitrary na positibong integer na $n$.\n"
"Tulad ng Deutsch's problem, ang gawain ay mag-output ng $0$ kung ang $f$ ay constant at $1$ kung ang $f$ ay balanced, na nangangahulugang ang bilang ng mga input string kung saan ang function ay kumukuha ng halagang $0$ ay katumbas ng bilang ng mga input string kung saan ang function ay kumukuha ng halagang $1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that, when $n$ is larger than $1$, there are functions of the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ that are neither constant nor balanced.\n"
"For example, the function $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin na, kapag ang $n$ ay mas malaki sa $1$, mayroong mga function ng anyo $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ na hindi constant at hindi rin balanced.\n"
"Halimbawa, ang function na $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ na tinukoy bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"falls into neither of these two categories.\n"
"For the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, we simply don't worry about functions like this — they're considered to be \"don't care\" inputs.\n"
"That is, for this problem we have a *promise* that $f$ is either constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay hindi nahuhulog sa alinman sa dalawang kategoryang ito.\n"
"Para sa Deutsch-Jozsa problem, hindi na natin alalahanin ang mga ganitong function — itinuturing itong mga \"don't care\" na input.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, para sa problemang ito mayroon tayong *pangako* na ang $f$ ay constant o balanced.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch-Jozsa problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: $f$ is either constant or balanced \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch-Jozsa problem\">\n"
"Input: isang function na $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Pangako: ang $f$ ay constant o balanced \\\n"
"Output: $0$ kung ang $f$ ay constant, $1$ kung ang $f$ ay balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, with its single query, solves this problem in the following sense:\n"
"if every one of the $n$ measurement outcomes is $0$, then the function $f$ is constant;\n"
"and otherwise, if at least one of the measurement outcomes is $1$, then the function $f$ is balanced.\n"
"Another way to say this is that the circuit described above is followed by a classical post-processing step in which the OR of the measurement outcomes is computed to produce the output bit of the Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, sa iisang query nito, ay nilulutas ang problemang ito sa sumusunod na paraan:\n"
"kung lahat ng $n$ na resulta ng pagsukat ay $0$, kung gayon ang function na $f$ ay constant;\n"
"at kung hindi, kapag hindi bababa sa isa sa mga resulta ng pagsukat ay $1$, kung gayon ang function na $f$ ay balanced.\n"
"Isa pang paraan ng pagsasabi nito ay ang circuit na inilarawan sa itaas ay sinusundan ng classical post-processing na hakbang kung saan kinukuwenta ang OR ng mga resulta ng pagsukat upang makabuo ng output bit ng Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis}"
msgstr "Pagsusuri ng algorithm {#algorithm-analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze the performance of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, it's helpful to begin by thinking about the action of a single layer of Hadamard gates.\n"
"A Hadamard operation can be expressed as a matrix in the usual way,\n"
msgstr ""
"Para masuri ang pagganap ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm para sa Deutsch-Jozsa problem, makakatulong na magsimula sa pag-iisip tungkol sa kilos ng isang layer ng mga Hadamard gate.\n"
"Ang isang Hadamard na operasyon ay maaaring ipahayag bilang isang matrix sa karaniwang paraan,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "but we can also express this operation in terms of its action on standard basis states:\n"
msgstr "ngunit maaari rin nating ipahayag ang operasyong ito sa pamamagitan ng kilos nito sa mga standard basis state:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These two equations can be combined into a single formula,\n"
msgstr "Ang dalawang ekwasyong ito ay maaaring pagsamahin sa isang formula,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is true for both choices of $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr "na totoo para sa parehong pagpipilian ng $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose that instead of just a single qubit we have $n$ qubits, and a Hadamard operation is performed on each.\n"
"The combined operation on the $n$ qubits is described by the tensor product $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ times), which we write as $H^{\\otimes n}$ for conciseness and clarity.\n"
"Using the formula from above, followed by expanding and then simplifying, we can express the action of this combined operation on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, ipagpalagay na sa halip na isang qubit lamang ay mayroon tayong $n$ na qubit, at isang Hadamard na operasyon ay isinasagawa sa bawat isa.\n"
"Ang pinagsama-samang operasyon sa $n$ na qubit ay inilarawan ng tensor product na $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ beses), na isinusulat natin bilang $H^{\\otimes n}$ para sa kaiklian at kalinawan.\n"
"Gamit ang formula mula sa itaas, sinusundan ng pagpapalawak at pagpapasimple, maaari nating ipahayag ang kilos ng pinagsama-samang operasyong ito sa mga standard basis state ng $n$ qubit tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, by the way, we're writing binary strings of length $n$ as $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$, following Qiskit's indexing convention.\n"
msgstr "Dito, sa pamamagitan ng paraan, isinusulat natin ang mga binary string na may haba na $n$ bilang $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ at $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$, sumusunod sa indexing convention ng Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula provides us with a useful tool for analyzing the quantum circuit above.\n"
"After the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits (including the leftmost/bottom qubit, which is treated separately from the rest) is\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang formula na ito ay nagbibigay sa atin ng kapaki-pakinabang na kasangkapan para suriin ang quantum circuit sa itaas.\n"
"Pagkatapos isagawa ang unang layer ng mga Hadamard gate, ang estado ng $n+1$ na qubit (kasama ang pinakakaliwang/pinakamababang qubit, na tinatrato nang hiwalay mula sa iba) ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the $U_f$ operation is performed, this state is transformed into\n"
msgstr "Kapag isinagawa ang operasyong $U_f$, ang estado ay nababago sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "through exactly the same phase kick-back phenomenon that we saw in the analysis of Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "sa pamamagitan ng parehong phase kick-back na penomenon na nakita natin sa pagsusuri ng algorithm ni Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the second layer of Hadamard gates is performed, which (by the formula above) transforms this state into\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ay isinasagawa ang ikalawang layer ng mga Hadamard gate, na (ayon sa formula sa itaas) ay nagbabago ng estado na ito sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This expression looks somewhat complicated, and not too much can be concluded about the probabilities to obtain different measurement outcomes without knowing more about the function $f$.\n"
msgstr "Medyo kumplikado ang hitsura ng ekspresyong ito, at hindi masyadong maraming masasabi tungkol sa mga probabilidad na makuha ang iba't ibang resulta ng pagsukat nang hindi alam pa ang higit pa tungkol sa function na $f$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fortunately, all we need to know is the probability that every one of the measurement outcomes is $0$ — because that's the probability that the algorithm determines that $f$ is constant.\n"
"This probability has a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kabutihang palad, ang kailangan lang nating malaman ay ang probabilidad na lahat ng resulta ng pagsukat ay $0$ — dahil iyon ang probabilidad na matukoy ng algorithm na ang $f$ ay constant.\n"
"Ang probabilidad na ito ay may simpleng formula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $f$ is constant}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{if $f$ is balanced}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $f$ is constant}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{if $f$ is balanced}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that these values correspond to the probability of measuring the state\n"
"$\\vert 0^{\\otimes n} \\rangle$, rather than directly to the final classical output bit of\n"
"the Deutsch-Jozsa problem. The algorithm outputs $0$ when all measurement\n"
"outcomes are $0$ (indicating that $f$ is constant), and outputs $1$ otherwise\n"
"(indicating that $f$ is balanced).\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang mga value na ito ay tumutugma sa probability ng pagsukat sa state\n"
"$\\vert 0^{\\otimes n} \\rangle$, sa halip na direkta sa huling classical output bit ng\n"
"Deutsch-Jozsa problem. Ang algorithm ay naglalabas ng $0$ kapag lahat ng measurement\n"
"outcome ay $0$ (na nagpapahiwatig na ang $f$ ay constant), at naglalabas ng $1$ sa ibang pagkakataon\n"
"(na nagpapahiwatig na ang $f$ ay balanced).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, if $f$ is constant, then either $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $2^n$, or $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $-2^n$.\n"
"Dividing by $2^n$ and taking the square of the absolute value yields $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mas detalyadong paliwanag, kung ang $f$ ay constant, kung gayon alinman ay $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ para sa bawat string na $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"kung saan ang halaga ng sum ay $2^n$, o kaya ay $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ para sa bawat string na $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"kung saan ang halaga ng sum ay $-2^n$.\n"
"Sa pag-divide ng $2^n$ at pagkuha ng parisukat ng absolute value ay nakukuha natin ang $1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If, on the other hand, $f$ is balanced, then $f$ takes the value $0$ on half of the strings $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and the value $1$ on the other half, so the $+1$ terms and $-1$ terms in the sum cancel and we're left with the value $0$.\n"
msgstr "Kung, sa kabilang banda, ang $f$ ay balanced, kung gayon ang $f$ ay kumukuha ng halagang $0$ sa kalahati ng mga string na $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ at halagang $1$ sa kabilang kalahati, kaya ang mga $+1$ at $-1$ na termino sa sum ay nagkakansela at natitira tayo sa halagang $0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We conclude that the algorithm operates correctly provided that the promise is fulfilled.\n"
msgstr "Napagtatanto natin na ang algorithm ay gumagana nang tama basta natutupad ang pangako.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty}"
msgstr "Kahirapan sa classical {#classical-difficulty}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm works every time, always giving us the correct answer when the promise is met, and requires a single query.\n"
"How does this compare with classical query algorithms for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem?\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm ay gumagana sa bawat pagkakataon, laging nagbibigay ng tamang sagot kapag natutupad ang pangako, at nangangailangan ng isang query lamang.\n"
"Paano ito ikukumpara sa classical query algorithm para sa Deutsch-Jozsa problem?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, any *deterministic* classical algorithm that correctly solves the Deutsch-Jozsa problem must make exponentially many queries:\n"
"$2^{n-1} + 1$ queries are required in the worst case.\n"
"The reasoning is that, if a deterministic algorithm queries $f$ on $2^{n-1}$ or fewer different strings, and obtains the same function value every time, then both answers are still possible.\n"
"The function might be constant, or it might be balanced but through bad luck the queries all happen to return the same function value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, ang anumang *deterministic* na classical algorithm na wastong nalulutas ng Deutsch-Jozsa problem ay dapat gumawa ng exponential na maraming query:\n"
"kailangan ang $2^{n-1} + 1$ na query sa pinakamasamang kaso.\n"
"Ang dahilan ay, kung ang isang deterministic na algorithm ay nag-query sa $f$ sa $2^{n-1}$ o mas kaunting iba't ibang string, at nakakakuha ng parehong function value sa bawat pagkakataon, kung gayon parehong sagot ay posible pa rin.\n"
"Ang function ay maaaring constant, o maaaring balanced ngunit sa malas ang mga query ay nagbabalik ng parehong function value.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second possibility might seem unlikely — but for deterministic algorithms there's no randomness or uncertainty, so they will fail systematically on certain functions.\n"
"We therefore have a significant advantage of quantum over classical algorithms in this regard.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ikalawang posibilidad ay maaaring mukhang hindi malamang — ngunit para sa mga deterministic na algorithm ay walang randomness o kawalan ng katiyakan, kaya mabibigo sila nang sistematiko sa ilang mga function.\n"
"Kaya naman mayroon tayong makabuluhang kalamangan ng quantum kumpara sa classical na algorithm sa aspetong ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is a catch, however, which is that *probabilistic* classical algorithms can solve the Deutsch-Jozsa problem with very high probability using just a few queries.\n"
"In particular, if we simply choose a few different strings of length $n$ randomly, and query $f$ on those strings, it's unlikely that we'll get the same function value for all of them when $f$ is balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngunit mayroon isang caveat, at iyon ay ang mga *probabilistic* na classical algorithm ay kayang malutas ang Deutsch-Jozsa problem nang may napakataas na probabilidad gamit ang ilang query lamang.\n"
"Sa partikular, kung pipili lang tayo ng ilang iba't ibang string na may haba na $n$ nang random, at mag-query sa $f$ sa mga string na iyon, hindi malamang na makakakuha tayo ng parehong function value para sa lahat ng mga ito kapag ang $f$ ay balanced.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be specific, if we choose $k$ input strings $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ uniformly at random, evaluate $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k)$, and answer $0$ if the function values are all the same, and $1$ if not, then we'll always be correct when $f$ is constant, and wrong in the case that $f$ is balanced with probability just $2^{-k + 1}$.\n"
"If we take $k = 11$, for instance, this algorithm will answer correctly with probability greater than $99.9$%.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para maging tiyak, kung pipiliin natin ang $k$ na input string na $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ nang uniformly at random, suriin ang $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k)$, at sumagot ng $0$ kung pareho ang lahat ng function value, at $1$ kung hindi, palagi tayong magiging tama kapag ang $f$ ay constant, at maling sagot sa kaso ng balanced na $f$ na may probabilidad na $2^{-k + 1}$ lamang.\n"
"Kung kukuha tayo ng $k = 11$, halimbawa, ang algorithm na ito ay sasagot nang tama nang may probabilidad na mas malaki sa $99.9$%.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this reason, we do still have a rather modest advantage of quantum over classical algorithms — but it is nevertheless a quantifiable advantage representing an improvement over Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Dahil dito, mayroon pa rin tayong medyo maliit na kalamangan ng quantum kumpara sa classical na algorithm — ngunit ito ay isang nasusukat na kalamangan na kumakatawan sa pagpapabuti kumpara sa algorithm ni Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch-Jozsa with Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Deutsch-Jozsa gamit ang Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm in Qiskit, we'll start by defining a function `dj_query` that generates a quantum circuit implementing a query gate, for a randomly selected function satisfying the promise for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"
"With a 50% chance, the function is constant, and with 50% change the function is balanced.\n"
"For each of those two possibilities, the function is selected uniformly from the functions of that type.\n"
"The argument is the number of input bits of the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ipatupad ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm sa Qiskit, magsisimula tayo sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy ng function na `dj_query` na gumagawa ng quantum circuit na nagpapatupad ng query gate, para sa isang random na piniling function na nakakatugon sa pangako para sa Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"
"Sa 50% na tsansa, ang function ay constant, at sa 50% na tsansa ang function ay balanced.\n"
"Para sa bawat isa sa dalawang posibilidad na iyon, ang function ay pinipili nang uniformly mula sa mga function ng ganoong uri.\n"
"Ang argument ay ang bilang ng input bits ng function.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can show the quantum circuit implementation of the query gate using the `draw` method as usual.\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating ipakita ang quantum circuit na implementasyon ng query gate gamit ang `draw` na paraan tulad ng dati.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next we define a function that creates the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit, taking a quantum circuit implementation of a query gate as an argument.\n"
msgstr "Susunod na tutukuyin natin ang isang function na gumagawa ng Deutsch-Jozsa circuit, na tumatanggap ng quantum circuit na implementasyon ng query gate bilang argument.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit once is defined.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, isang function na nagpapatakbo ng Deutsch-Jozsa circuit nang isang beses ay tinukoy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can test our implementation by choosing a function randomly, displaying the quantum circuit implementation of a query gate for this function, and then running the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm on that function.\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating subukan ang ating implementasyon sa pamamagitan ng random na pagpili ng function, pagpapakita ng quantum circuit na implementasyon ng query gate para sa function na ito, at pagpapatakbo ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm sa function na iyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/aca4745e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/aca4745e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Bernstein-Vazirani problem {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"
msgstr "Ang Bernstein-Vazirani problem {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we'll discuss a problem known as the *Bernstein-Vazirani problem*.\n"
"It's also called the *Fourier sampling problem*, although there are more general formulations of this problem that also go by that name.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, tatalakayin natin ang isang problem na kilala bilang ang *Bernstein-Vazirani problem*.\n"
"Tinatawag din itong *Fourier sampling problem*, kahit mayroon pa ring mas pangkalahatang mga formulation ng problemang ito na tinatawag rin sa pangalang iyon.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's introduce some notation.\n"
"For any two binary strings $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ and $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ of length $n$, we define\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, ipakilala natin ang ilang notasyon.\n"
"Para sa anumang dalawang binary string na $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ at $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ na may haba na $n$, tinutukoy natin ang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll refer to this operation as the *binary dot product*.\n"
"An alternative way to define it is like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tatawagin natin ang operasyong ito bilang ang *binary dot product*.\n"
"Isang alternatibong paraan ng pagtukoy nito ay ganito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is odd}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is even}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is odd}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is even}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that this is a symmetric operation, meaning that the result doesn't change if we swap $x$ and $y$, so we're free to do that whenever it's convenient.\n"
"Sometimes it's useful to think about the binary dot product $x \\cdot y$ as being the parity of the bits of $x$ in positions where the string $y$ has a $1$, or equivalently, the parity of the bits of $y$ in positions where the string $x$ has a $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin na ito ay isang symmetric na operasyon, ibig sabihin, ang resulta ay hindi nagbabago kung i-swap natin ang $x$ at $y$, kaya malaya tayong gawin ito anumang oras na maginhawa.\n"
"Minsan ay kapaki-pakinabang na isipin ang binary dot product na $x \\cdot y$ bilang ang parity ng mga bit ng $x$ sa mga posisyon kung saan ang string na $y$ ay may $1$, o katumbas nito, ang parity ng mga bit ng $y$ sa mga posisyon kung saan ang string na $x$ ay may $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this notation in hand we can now define the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"
msgstr "Sa notasyong ito, maaari na nating tukuyin ang Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Bernstein-Vazirani problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: there exists a binary string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ for which $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for all $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: the string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Bernstein-Vazirani problem\">\n"
"Input: isang function na $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Pangako: mayroon isang binary string na $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ kung saan ang $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ para sa lahat ng $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: ang string na $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We don't actually need a new quantum algorithm for this problem; the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm solves it.\n"
"In the interest of clarity, let's refer to the quantum circuit from above, which doesn't include the classical post-processing step of computing the OR, as the *Deutsch-Jozsa circuit*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi na natin kailangan ng bagong quantum algorithm para sa problemang ito; nilulutas ito ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"Para sa kalinawan, tukuyin natin ang quantum circuit mula sa itaas, na hindi kasama ang classical post-processing na hakbang ng pagkuwenta ng OR, bilang ang *Deutsch-Jozsa circuit*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis-1}"
msgstr "Pagsusuri ng algorithm {#algorithm-analysis-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze how the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit works for a function satisfying the promise for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, we'll begin with a quick observation.\n"
"Using the binary dot product, we can alternatively describe the action of $n$ Hadamard gates on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para masuri kung paano gumagana ang Deutsch-Jozsa circuit para sa isang function na nakakatugon sa pangako para sa Bernstein-Vazirani problem, magsisimula tayo sa isang mabilis na obserbasyon.\n"
"Gamit ang binary dot product, maaari nating alternatibong ilarawan ang kilos ng $n$ na Hadamard gate sa mga standard basis state ng $n$ qubit tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similar to what we saw when analyzing Deutsch's algorithm, this is because the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even or odd.\n"
msgstr "Katulad ng nakita natin nang sinusuri ang algorithm ni Deutsch, ito ay dahil ang halagang $(-1)^k$ para sa anumang integer na $k$ ay nakasalalay lamang sa kung ang $k$ ay even o odd.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turning to the Deutsch–Jozsa circuit, after the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits is\n"
msgstr "Bumabalik sa Deutsch–Jozsa circuit, pagkatapos isagawa ang unang layer ng mga Hadamard gate, ang estado ng $n+1$ na qubit ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The query gate is then performed, which (through the phase kickback phenomenon) transforms the state into\n"
msgstr "Ang query gate ay isinasagawa pagkatapos, na (sa pamamagitan ng phase kickback phenomenon) ay nagbabago ng estado sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using our formula for the action of a layer of Hadamard gates, we see that the second layer of Hadamard gates then transforms this state into\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang ating formula para sa kilos ng isang layer ng mga Hadamard gate, nakikita natin na ang ikalawang layer ng mga Hadamard gate ay nagbabago ng estado na ito sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can make some simplifications, in the exponent of $-1$ inside the sum.\n"
"We're promised that $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for some string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$, so we can express the state as\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay maaari tayong gumawa ng ilang simplipikasyon, sa exponent ng $-1$ sa loob ng sum.\n"
"Pinangako sa atin na ang $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ para sa ilang string na $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$, kaya maaari nating ipahayag ang estado bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $s\\cdot x$ and $x\\cdot y$ are binary values, we can replace the addition with the exclusive-OR — again because the only thing that matters for an integer in the exponent of $-1$ is whether it is even or odd.\n"
"Making use of the symmetry of the binary dot product, we obtain this expression for the state:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang $s\\cdot x$ at $x\\cdot y$ ay mga binary na halaga, maaari nating palitan ang addition ng exclusive-OR — muli dahil ang tanging mahalaga para sa isang integer sa exponent ng $-1$ ay kung ito ay even o odd.\n"
"Gamit ang symmetry ng binary dot product, makukuha natin ang ekspresyong ito para sa estado:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Parentheses have been added for clarity, though they aren't really necessary because it's conventional to treat the binary dot product as having higher precedence than the exclusive-OR.)\n"
msgstr "(Ang mga panaklong ay idinagdag para sa kalinawan, kahit hindi talaga kailangan dahil kaugalian na tratuhin ang binary dot product na may mas mataas na precedence kaysa sa exclusive-OR.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point we will make use of the following formula.\n"
msgstr "Sa puntong ito gagamitin natin ang sumusunod na formula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can obtain the formula through a similar formula for bits,\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating makuha ang formula sa pamamagitan ng katulad na formula para sa mga bit,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "together with an expansion of the binary dot product and bitwise exclusive-OR:\n"
msgstr "kasama ang pagpapalawak ng binary dot product at bitwise exclusive-OR:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This allows us to express the state of the circuit immediately prior to the measurements like this:\n"
msgstr "Ito ay nagpapahintulot sa atin na ipahayag ang estado ng circuit bago pa ang mga pagsukat tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The final step is to make use of yet another formula, which works for every binary string $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0$.\n"
msgstr "Ang huling hakbang ay gamitin ang isa pang formula, na gumagana para sa bawat binary string na $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{if $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{if $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we're using a simple notation for strings that we'll use several more times in the lesson: $0^n$ is the all-zero string of length $n$.\n"
msgstr "Dito gumagamit tayo ng simpleng notasyon para sa mga string na gagamitin natin ng ilang beses pa sa aralin: ang $0^n$ ay ang all-zero string na may haba na $n.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple way to argue that this formula works is to consider the two cases separately.\n"
"If $z = 0^n$, then $z\\cdot x = 0$ for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, so the value of each term in the sum is $1$, and we obtain $1$ by summing and dividing by $2^n$.\n"
"On the other hand, if any one of the bits of $z$ is equal to $1$, then the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ is equal to $0$ for exactly half of the possible choices for $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ and $1$ for the other half — because the value of the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ flips (from $0$ to $1$ or from $1$ to $0$) if we flip any bit of $x$ in a position where $z$ has a $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang simpleng paraan para ipakita na gumagana ang formula na ito ay ang isaalang-alang ang dalawang kaso nang hiwalay.\n"
"Kung ang $z = 0^n$, kung gayon ang $z\\cdot x = 0$ para sa bawat string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, kaya ang halaga ng bawat termino sa sum ay $1$, at nakakakuha tayo ng $1$ sa pamamagitan ng pagdaragdag at pag-divide ng $2^n$.\n"
"Sa kabilang banda, kung ang alinman sa mga bit ng $z$ ay katumbas ng $1$, kung gayon ang binary dot product na $z\\cdot x$ ay katumbas ng $0$ para sa eksakto sa kalahati ng mga posibleng pagpipilian para sa $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ at $1$ para sa kabilang kalahati — dahil ang halaga ng binary dot product na $z\\cdot x$ ay nagbabago (mula $0$ hanggang $1$ o mula $1$ hanggang $0$) kung i-flip natin ang anumang bit ng $x$ sa isang posisyon kung saan ang $z$ ay may $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we now apply this formula to simplify the state of the circuit prior to the measurements, we obtain\n"
msgstr "Kung ilalapat natin ang formula na ito para pasimplehin ang estado ng circuit bago ang mga pagsukat, makukuha natin ang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"owing to the fact that $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ if and only if $y = s$.\n"
"Thus, the measurements reveal precisely the string $s$ we're looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"dahil sa katotohanang ang $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ kung at kung ang $y = s$.\n"
"Kaya, ang mga pagsukat ay nagpapakita ng eksakto ang string na $s$ na hinahanap natin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty-1}"
msgstr "Kahirapan sa classical {#classical-difficulty-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit solves the Bernstein-Vazirani problem with a single query, any classical query algorithm must make at least $n$ queries to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr "Habang nilulutas ng Deutsch-Jozsa circuit ang Bernstein-Vazirani problem gamit ang isang query, ang anumang classical query algorithm ay kailangang gumawa ng hindi bababa sa $n$ na query para malutas ang problemang ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be reasoned through a so-called *information theoretic* argument, which is very simple in this case.\n"
"Each classical query reveals a single bit of information about the solution, and there are $n$ bits of information that need to be uncovered — so at least $n$ queries are needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari itong ipaliwanag sa pamamagitan ng tinatawag na *information theoretic* na argumento, na napakasimple sa kasong ito.\n"
"Ang bawat classical query ay nagbubunyag ng isang bit ng impormasyon tungkol sa solusyon, at mayroon $n$ na bit ng impormasyon na kailangang matuklasan — kaya kailangan ng hindi bababa sa $n$ na query.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, in fact, possible to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem classically by querying the function on each of the $n$ strings having a single $1$, in each possible position, and $0$ for all other bits, which reveals the bits of $s$ one at a time.\n"
"Therefore, the advantage of quantum over classical algorithms for this problem is $1$ query versus $n$ queries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa katunayan, posible na malutas ang Bernstein-Vazirani problem nang klasikal sa pamamagitan ng pag-query sa function sa bawat isa sa $n$ na string na may isang $1$, sa bawat posibleng posisyon, at $0$ para sa lahat ng iba pang bit, na nagbubunyag ng mga bit ng $s$ nang isa-isa.\n"
"Kaya naman, ang kalamangan ng quantum kumpara sa classical na algorithm para sa problemang ito ay $1$ query kumpara sa $n$ na query.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bernstein-Vazirani with Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Bernstein-Vazirani gamit ang Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've already implemented the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit above, and here we will make use of it to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"
"First we'll define a function that implements a query gate for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem given any binary string $s$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Naipatupad na natin ang Deutsch-Jozsa circuit sa itaas, at dito gagamitin natin ito para malutas ang Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"
"Una, tutukuyin natin ang isang function na nagpapatupad ng query gate para sa Bernstein-Vazirani problem para sa anumang binary string na $s$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can create a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit on the function, using the `compile_circuit` function that was defined previously.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay maaari tayong lumikha ng isang function na nagpapatakbo ng Deutsch-Jozsa circuit sa function, gamit ang `compile_circuit` na function na tinukoy nang mas maaga.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remark on nomenclature {#remark-on-nomenclature}"
msgstr "Puna sa nomenclature {#remark-on-nomenclature}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, it is common that the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm is referred to as the \"Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm.\"\n"
"This is slightly misleading, because the algorithm *is* the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, as Bernstein and Vazirani were very clear about in their work.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa konteksto ng Bernstein-Vazirani problem, karaniwang tinutukoy ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm bilang \"Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm.\"\n"
"Ito ay bahagyang nakakalito, dahil ang algorithm *ay* ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, gaya ng malinaw na itinakda nina Bernstein at Vazirani sa kanilang gawain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bernstein and Vazirani did after showing that the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm solves the Bernstein-Vazirani problem (as it is stated above) was to define a much more complicated problem, known as the *recursive Fourier sampling problem*.\n"
"This is a highly contrived problem where solutions to different instances of the problem effectively unlock new levels of the problem arranged in a tree-like structure.\n"
"The Bernstein-Vazirani problem is essentially just the base case of this more complicated problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ginawa nina Bernstein at Vazirani pagkatapos ipakita na nilulutas ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm ang Bernstein-Vazirani problem (tulad ng nakasaad sa itaas) ay tumukoy ng mas kumplikadong problema, na kilala bilang ang *recursive Fourier sampling problem*.\n"
"Ito ay isang lubhang contrived na problema kung saan ang mga solusyon sa iba't ibang instance ng problema ay epektibong nagbubukas ng mga bagong antas ng problema na nakaayos sa isang tree-like na istraktura.\n"
"Ang Bernstein-Vazirani problem ay mahalagang base case lamang ng mas kumplikadong problemang ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The recursive Fourier sampling problem was the first known example of a query problem where quantum algorithms have a so-called *super-polynomial* advantage over probabilistic algorithms, thereby surpassing the advantage of quantum over classical offered by the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the recursive version of the problem amplifies the $1$ versus $n$ advantage of quantum algorithms to something much larger.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang recursive Fourier sampling problem ay ang unang kilalang halimbawa ng isang query problem kung saan ang mga quantum algorithm ay may tinatawag na *super-polynomial* na kalamangan kumpara sa mga probabilistic na algorithm, na lumagpas sa kalamangan ng quantum kumpara sa classical na inaalok ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"Sa intuitive na pagsasalita, ang recursive na bersyon ng problema ay nagpapalaki ng $1$ kumpara sa $n$ na kalamangan ng mga quantum algorithm sa mas malaking bagay.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most challenging aspect of the mathematical analysis establishing this advantage is showing that classical query algorithms can't solve the problem without making lots of queries.\n"
"This is quite typical; for many problems it can be very difficult to rule out creative classical approaches that solve them efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pinaka-mapaghamong aspeto ng mathematical analysis na nagtatag ng kalamantang ito ay ang pagpapakita na ang mga classical query algorithm ay hindi makakalutas ng problema nang hindi gumagawa ng maraming query.\n"
"Ito ay napaka-tipikal; para sa maraming problema maaaring maging napakahirap na ibukod ang mga malikhaing classical na diskarte na naglulutas sa kanila nang mahusay.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simon's problem, and the algorithm for it described in the next section, does provide a much simpler example of a super-polynomial (and, in fact, exponential) advantage of quantum over classical algorithms, and for this reason the recursive Fourier sampling problem is less often discussed.\n"
"It is, nevertheless, an interesting computational problem in its own right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Simon's problem, at ang algorithm para dito na inilarawan sa susunod na seksyon, ay nagbibigay ng mas simpleng halimbawa ng isang super-polynomial (at, sa katunayan, exponential) na kalamangan ng quantum kumpara sa classical na algorithm, at sa kadahilanang ito ang recursive Fourier sampling problem ay hindi gaanong madalas na tinalakay.\n"
"Ito ay, gayunpaman, isang kawili-wiling computational problem sa sarili nitong karapatan.\n"
